course: dictionary
lesson: 7382
title: Plughole and the words around it
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word's context is the words and sentences around it, and they often give clues to its meaning. «A spider in the bath has usually fallen in and cannot climb out, because the sides are too smooth; it did not come up the plughole.» The spider did not come up the plughole, so the plughole must be a hole that leads down, where the water goes.
explain: Test your meaning by putting it into the sentence. The dictionary says a plughole is the hole at the bottom of a bath or sink where water drains away. Try it: «Find a big spider in the bath and it looks as if it crawled up the plughole.» The meaning fits, so you can trust it.
explain: Words change from place to place. People in Britain, Ireland, Australia and New Zealand say plughole, but Americans say drain for the same hole. When the context does not tell you enough, check a dictionary.
fact: A plughole is the hole at the bottom of a bath or sink where water drains away.
fact: Hair can block the plughole, so the water stays in the bath.
fact: A plug goes into the plughole to keep water in.
fact: Water spinning down a plughole can form a little whirlpool.
fact: «Go down the plughole» means to be wasted or lost.
exercise: «A spider in the bath has usually fallen in and cannot climb out, because the sides are too smooth; it did not come up the plughole.» What is a plughole? | A small towel for drying feet | A kind of spider | A tap that makes hot water | * The hole at the bottom of a bath or sink where water drains away
exercise: Sam says «go down the plughole» means to go down a slide. What does it really mean? | To fall into the bath | To slide down quickly | * To be wasted or lost | To find something new
exercise: «Find a big spider in the bath and it looks as if it crawled up the plughole.» What does crawled mean? | * Moved slowly close to the ground | Swam fast in the water | Jumped high into the air | Flew across the room
test: Hair can block the plughole. What happens to the water in the bath if the plughole is blocked? | * The water stays in the bath | The water flies out of the bath | The plug disappears | The bath gets cleaner
test: A plug goes into the plughole to keep water in. What does a plug do? | Makes the water hot | Makes the bath colder | * Keeps water in the bath or sink | Lets water out very fast
exam: Why might someone in America call a plughole a drain? | Because a plughole is a kind of spider | Because a drain is always made of gold | Because plugholes are only found in America | * Because Americans say drain for the same hole
